Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 07:40:59 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 039/159] [ae-patch] Fix the review findings on the calmer pull
 request cards

The dual review of the card redesign (Codex and Claude, 2026-10-14) found
two things in the chat card that Reid asked to fix.

A card with no data yet (still reading GitHub, or the read failed) showed
the green open-pull-request icon and told screen readers "Open pull
request" before anyone knew the state. It now shows a muted
git-pull-request icon labelled "Pull request" until the card arrives.

On a narrow card Cancel and the confirm button each took half the row.
The confirm button now names the branch ("Squash into release/2026.10"),
so Cancel stays compact and the confirm button takes the rest, the same
row the Dashboard draws.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
